Negative-s values (= pentanacci traces):
  Tr(M₅^n) = [5, 1, 3, 7, 15, 31, 57, 113, 223, 439, 863, 1695, 3333, 6553, 12883]
  Primes in sequence: n=0:5 n=2:3 n=3:7 n=5:31 n=7:113 n=8:223 n=9:439 n=10:863 n=13:6553 

If (2, 3, 5) generates forbidden H values ζ_M₃(-3)=7 and ζ_M₃(-5)=21,
what does (2, 5, Ellipsis) generate?

The pentanacci trace at n=3: 7
The pentanacci trace at n=5: 31

For comparison:
  Tribonacci traces: 3, 1, 3, 7, 11, 21, 39, 71, 131, ...
  Pentanacci traces: [5, 1, 3, 7, 15, 31, 57, 113, 223, 439, 863, 1695, 3333, 6553, 12883]

The pentanacci trace at the "directed scales" (n=3, 5):
  ζ_{M₅}(-3) = 7
  ζ_{M₅}(-5) = 31

These would be the "forbidden" values in a pentanacci theory.

